{% extends "layout/base.njk" %}

{% block content %}

<!-- Hero -->
<section class="dest-page-hero" id="top">

  <div class="dest-page-hero__img">
    <div class="photo-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="dest-page-hero__overlay"></div>

  <nav class="dest-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <div class="dest-breadcrumb__inner">
      <a href="/" class="dest-breadcrumb__link">Home</a>
      <span class="dest-breadcrumb__sep">&rsaquo;</span>
      <span class="dest-breadcrumb__current">Walt Disney World</span>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <div class="dest-page-hero__content">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">Walt Disney World</p>
    <h1 class="dest-page-hero__headline">
      The Most Magical Place on Earth,<br>
      planned <em>right.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="dest-page-hero__sub">
      Four parks, two water parks, Disney Springs, and a resort strategy that can make or break your entire trip. I've been here with my family at every stage — and I'll make sure your trip is everything you pictured.
    </p>
    <a href="{{ site.links.consultation }}" class="btn btn--gold" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Start Your Escape
    </a>
  </div>

</section>

<!-- Personal Story -->
<section class="dest-story" id="our-experience">
  <div class="dest-story__inner">

    <div class="dest-story__text reveal">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Our Experience</p>
      <h2 class="dest-story__headline">
        A theme park trip like<br>
        <em>no other.</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="dest-story__body">
        Walt Disney World was the trip that changed how I think about family vacations. We arrived thinking we knew what to expect — a theme park is a theme park, right? We were wrong. The scale, the storytelling, the way Disney makes every member of the family feel like the experience was made for them specifically — it's unlike anything else.
      </p>
      <p class="dest-story__body">
        I've been multiple times now, with different ages, different group sizes, and different budgets. What I've learned is that the difference between a great Disney trip and an overwhelming one comes down almost entirely to planning. The right resort, the right park order, the right strategy for Lightning Lane — these decisions compound.
      </p>
      <p class="dest-story__body">
        My job is to make all of those decisions for you so that when you walk through those gates, the only thing on your mind is being present for the moments that matter.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="dest-story__photo reveal">
      <div class="photo-placeholder" aria-label="Chuck's family at Walt Disney World"></div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- Insider Tips -->
<section class="dest-tips" id="tips">
  <div class="dest-tips__inner">

    <div class="dest-tips__header reveal">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">What I've Learned</p>
      <h2 class="dest-tips__headline">
        Insider tips from<br>
        someone who's <em>been there.</em>
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="dest-tips__grid">

      <article class="dest-tip reveal">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">01</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Book Your Resort Before Your Tickets</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">Resort selection shapes everything: which parks you can walk to, when you can rope drop, what transportation you're dealing with. Don't pick tickets first — your resort is the foundation of the whole trip.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip reveal">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">02</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Rope Drop Is Your Best Friend</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">Getting to the park 30 minutes before official open isn't just about shorter lines. It's the only time of day the park feels like it belongs to you. The difference between 7am and 10am at Magic Kingdom is staggering.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip reveal">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">03</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Lightning Lane: Selectively, Not Everything</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">You don't need it for every ride. Use it strategically for the two or three headliners per park and rope drop the rest. Buying it for everything is expensive and rarely necessary with good planning.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip reveal">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">04</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">EPCOT Hits Different as an Adult</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">Most first-timers rush through EPCOT or skip it. It's my favorite park — World Showcase, the food, the festivals. If you're going as a couple or with older kids, give it a full day. You won't regret it.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip reveal">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">05</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Monorail Resorts Change Everything</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">Staying at the Contemporary, Polynesian, or Grand Floridian means Magic Kingdom is a short walk or monorail ride away. That changes your morning, your evening fireworks view, and your whole daily rhythm.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="dest-tip reveal">
        <span class="dest-tip__num">06</span>
        <h3 class="dest-tip__title">Build In Rest. Seriously.</h3>
        <p class="dest-tip__body">A full Disney itinerary without breaks will wreck you by day three. A pool afternoon or a lazy Disney Springs morning isn't wasted time — it's what makes the rest of the trip sustainable and genuinely enjoyable.</p>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Gallery -->
<section class="dest-gallery" id="gallery">
  <div class="dest-gallery__inner">

    <div class="dest-gallery__header reveal">
      <h2 class="dest-gallery__headline">Our Memories</h2>
      <p class="dest-gallery__note">Photos coming soon</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dest-gallery__grid">
      <figure class="dest-gallery__item">
        <div class="photo-placeholder" aria-label="Disney World photo coming soon"></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="dest-gallery__item">
        <div class="photo-placeholder" aria-label="Disney World photo coming soon"></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="dest-gallery__item">
        <div class="photo-placeholder" aria-label="Disney World photo coming soon"></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="dest-gallery__item">
        <div class="photo-placeholder" aria-label="Disney World photo coming soon"></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="dest-gallery__item">
        <div class="photo-placeholder" aria-label="Disney World photo coming soon"></div>
      </figure>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

{% include "partials/cta-strip.njk" %}

{% endblock %}
